fix: Disable Jetifier and add D8 class merging configuration as emergency fallback

Problem: Jetifier is transforming BOTH old support-compat:28.0.0 AND new androidx.core:1.16.0
to the same androidx.versionedparcelable namespace, causing D8 compiler to see
identical class definitions from both JAR files.

Solution:
1. Disable android.enableJetifier (set to false)
   - Prevents Jetifier from converting old support libs to androidx namespace
   - Old support lib classes will stay in com.android.support namespace
   - Should prevent duplicate androidx.versionedparcelable classes

2. Add D8 emergency class merging configuration
   - com.android.tools.r8.enableHorizontalClassMerging=true
   - Tells D8 to aggressively merge/deduplicate classes if needed
   - Last resort if exclusions still don't fully work

3. Expand packagingOptions pickFirsts pattern
   - Changed from individual class files to 'android/support/v4/**'
   - Catches entire v4 package if duplicates slip through
   - More robust pattern matching

Testing approach:
- Jetifier disabled means old support lib wont be auto-converted
- With exclusion rules in place, old lib should be filtered out entirely
- If old lib somehow reaches build, it should stay in com.android.support namespace,
  not androidx namespace, preventing duplicate class names
